# has no pull_request rule, so this file is advisory until the Sara-only
# required-flip step turns it on (see the PR that added the CI-surface block).
# Reviewers need write/admin access. GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from the PR's BASE
# branch, so a PR cannot edit this file to dodge its own review.

# Prod deploy configuration (Cloudflare)
/wrangler.jsonc                                @Sara3

# Deploy workflow
/.github/workflows/deploy.yml                  @Sara3

# CI surface [2026-10-02, savvy-backend#1595 / tracking #1239]. A same-repo PR can
# edit .github/workflows/gate.yml (or merge-guard.yml) to post the binding
# `opus-verdict-recorded` status itself with a GITHUB_TOKEN job, and nothing
# required runs from anywhere but the PR's own copy of the workflows. Code-owner
# review read from the base branch is the one guard a PR cannot edit, so it
# covers the whole CI surface (this also covers .github/CODEOWNERS and
# .github/dependabot.yml, and every dependabot action-bump PR).
/.github/                                      @Sara3
/.claude/scripts/                              @Sara3
